// =================================================================
// generation_data.js  —  EIA State Electricity Generation Data
// =================================================================
//
// HOW TO UPDATE
// -------------
// 1. Get a new EIA monthly generation CSV export.
// 2. Open this file in a text editor.
// 3. Select and delete everything between the two backtick lines.
// 4. Paste in your new CSV content (keep the header row).
// 5. Save and refresh the browser.
//
// REQUIRED COLUMNS  (order doesn't matter; extra columns ignored)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
//   Type       : Fuel type recognized values:
//                  Coal, Natural Gas, Nuclear, Hydro, Wind,
//                  Utility Solar, Distributed Solar,
//                  Petroleum, Other Fossil, Other Renewable
//   location   : 2-letter state code (e.g. CA, TX)
//                Rows where location = "US" are skipped.
//   period     : YYYY-MM  (e.g. 2024-01)
//   generation : Monthly net generation in GWh
//
// NOTES
// -----
// • Zero-generation rows can be omitted — they are treated as 0.
// • The dashboard recomputes rolling 12-month totals in the
//   browser automatically — no pre-processing needed.
// • Data should begin at least 12 months before the earliest
//   period you want visible in the chart.
// =================================================================

